  [1mB. A separate [38;5;153midentity.js[39m on a single global namespace.[0m New file exposing one object — [38;5;153mwindow.AppIdentity = { get, [39m
  [38;5;153mset, clear }[39m — loaded by a second [38;5;153m<script>[39m tag before [38;5;153mapp.js[39m. Future forms add the same tag and call it. [3mBuys:[0m works
  with exactly zero build tooling, which is this repo's real constraint; one file with one purpose; the future backend
  slots in behind an [38;5;153mauth.js[39m seam without touching callers. [3mCosts:[0m it's a global, and script order in the HTML becomes
  load-bearing. [3mRules out:[0m little — this migrates to modules cleanly if you ever add a build step.

  [1mC. Convert the browser half to ES modules.[0m [38;5;153m<script type="module" src="app.js">[39m, with [38;5;153midentity.js[39m using real
  [38;5;153mexport[39m/[38;5;153mimport[39m. [3mBuys:[0m genuine module boundaries, no globals, explicit dependencies, and a structure a test runner can
  import directly. [3mCosts:[0m ES modules don't load over [38;5;153mfile://[39m — opening [38;5;153mindex.html[39m by double-clicking stops working, so
  you'd need a local server ([38;5;153mpython3 -m http.server[39m or similar) for development. That's a workflow change, not just a
  code change. [3mRules out:[0m nothing, and it's where the app ends up eventually anyway.

  [1mMy recommendation: C[0m, with B as the fallback if the [38;5;153mfile://[39m cost is unacceptable. You've told me this needs to serve
  forms that don't exist yet, and C is the option where adding the second and third consumer costs one [38;5;153mimport[39m line
  instead of a script tag whose position matters. Modules are native in every current browser; the only real price is
  needing a local server, and any project that grows more pages pays that price soon regardless. If you regularly open
  [38;5;153mindex.html[39m straight from disk, that price is real and B gets you 90% of the benefit.

  One thing I'll need to flag in the design either way: with no backend, [38;5;153mlogin()[39m has to [3minvent[0m the user ID. I'll treat
  that as an explicit, labeled stub (deterministic per username, so the same person gets the same ID across logins) with
  a clear seam where the server-issued value replaces it — not as something that quietly looks real.
